+++ b/doc/src/api_plug.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+.. # Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Beartype authors.
+.. # See "LICENSE" for further details.
+
+################
+Beartype Plugins
+################
+
+Stateful runtime hints
+======================
+
+A runtime hint can opt into transactional checking by exposing a callable
+``__beartype_state__`` attribute. Calling it returns the library's active state
+object, which provides ``snapshot()`` and ``restore(token)`` methods. No beartype
+base class is required. The snapshot token can be any object, including None;
+beartype only passes it back to the corresponding restore method.
+
+This is useful for hints that bind named dimensions or other shared constraints.
+For ``tuple[N, str] | tuple[C, int]``, checking the first tuple may bind ``N``
+before discovering that the second item is not a string. That rejected
+alternative must discard its bindings before checking the second alternative.
+
+For example, a library managing a context-local state object can expose::
+
+    class ShapeState:
+        def __init__(self):
+            self.bindings = {}
+
+        def snapshot(self):
+            return self.bindings.copy()
+
+        def restore(self, before):
+            self.bindings.clear()
+            self.bindings.update(before)
+
+    def get_state():
+        return current_state.get()
+
+    class ShapeHintMeta(type):
+        __beartype_state__ = staticmethod(get_state)
+
+        def __instancecheck__(cls, value):
+            # Validate and bind dimensions in current_state.get().bindings.
+            ...
+
+Here, ``current_state`` is the library's context variable containing its active
+``ShapeState``. Hints sharing a state domain expose the **same getter object**.
+The getter locates state; it must not perform validation or mutate bindings.
+It returns a state object that remains valid throughout this checking expression.
+Beartype locates known domains once per expression and reuses their objects
+across union alternatives. Getters are deduplicated by identity. All methods
+are synchronous, and restore must restore the token without raising.
+
+The library owns state lifetime, including thread and task isolation. Cached
+hints and generated code must not retain any invocation's snapshots or argument
+objects. The getter may create invocation-local state if none exists yet.
+
+Transaction boundaries
+----------------------
+
+Successful alternatives retain state; rejected alternatives restore it before
+trying the next alternative. Failure of an outer alternative also undoes
+successful checks nested inside it. A failed parameter, return or DOOR check
+restores its entry state. Exceptions unwind all open checkpoints, including
+exceptions outside the stateful hint's own instance check. Successful earlier
+parameters remain bound if a later parameter fails.
+
+The implementation avoids a duplicate outer checkpoint when a top-level union's
+alternatives already protect the whole check. Leading stateless native
+alternatives can succeed before locating any state. These optimizations preserve
+existing alternative ordering, short-circuiting and container sampling. No
+alternative is evaluated twice. There is no backtracking to a different earlier
+parameter alternative, and sampling remains sampling.
+
+Diagnostics retain successful sibling bindings while explaining a failure,
+then restore all diagnostic changes. A later mismatch therefore reports the
+correct earlier dimension without leaving state in the caller's context.
+
+Discovery and forward references
+--------------------------------
+
+Beartype discovers the hook on classes reached by its sanitized hint traversal,
+including classes inside containers, generic bases and ``Annotated``. It does
+not introspect arbitrary Python predicates for hidden state changes.
+
+An evaluated lazy reference may introduce a domain after code generation. That
+domain joins open transactions before validation mutates it. Unselected
+references remain unresolved. A root reference delegates to its resolved hint;
+ordinary root references do not allocate a transaction. Nested expressions with
+unresolved references still require deferred transaction tracking. Context-local
+tracking keeps concurrent checks isolated. Copied contexts ignore finished
+checks, and finished checks release their state objects even when a copied
+context outlives them.
+
+Ordinary hints without participating classes or references retain their direct
+checking path. Transactional expressions are compiled once at decoration rather
+than allocating a checking closure on each invocation. Each checkpoint stores
+restore methods and opaque tokens; general exception-unwinding machinery is only
+needed if a plugin's restore method itself raises.
+
+Python's bare ``isinstance`` does not invoke this protocol. Libraries should
+preserve any individual-check guarantees they need outside beartype.
